WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350
Run Prompt two.

2
00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:07.125
Ask ChatGPT to prepare a metric contract
for revenue, transacting customers,

3
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:11.325
thirty-day activation, acquisition cost,
contribution margin and transaction

4
00:00:11.325 --> 00:00:11.850
success.

5
00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:17.619
For each one, inspect the formula, unit,
source location, reporting date and

6
00:00:17.619 --> 00:00:18.100
owner.

7
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.350
A convincing card can still use the wrong
denominator.

8
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.300
You approve the contract before building
the interface.

9
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.180
Treat missing inputs as missing; do not
let a plausible zero hide

10
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.400
an extraction problem.

11
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.400
When a required denominator is zero, the
rate is unavailable.

12
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.900
Start with June revenue.

13
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.625
The finance workbook records one hundred
and eighty thousand ringgit for

14
00:00:41.625 --> 00:00:45.920
web-acquired customers and four hundred
and twenty thousand for mobile-acquired

15
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:46.350
customers.

16
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.550
Together they produce six hundred thousand
ringgit.

17
00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:53.783
Revenue is Aura's company fee income, not
money held in customer wallets

18
00:00:53.783 --> 00:00:55.900
or the total value of payments.

19
00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:00.250
Variable costs total three hundred and
eighty-four thousand ringgit.

20
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:04.760
Revenue less those costs leaves two
hundred and sixteen thousand in

21
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.400
contribution, or thirty-six percent.

22
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.686
Acquisition spending and fixed overhead
are excluded, so this margin is not

23
00:01:10.686 --> 00:01:11.400
net profit.

24
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.800
June has ten thousand newly verified
customers.

25
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.433
Three thousand eight hundred of that
acquisition-month cohort complete their

26
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:21.750
first transaction within thirty days.

27
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.950
Activation is therefore thirty-eight
percent.

28
00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:30.027
The acquisition budget spent in June is
six hundred and sixty thousand

29
00:01:30.027 --> 00:01:30.450
ringgit.

30
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:35.507
Dividing by new verified customers gives a
cost of sixty-six ringgit per

31
00:01:35.507 --> 00:01:36.350
verified customer.

32
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:41.104
Dividing by activated customers gives
about one hundred and seventy-four ringgit

33
00:01:41.104 --> 00:01:42.400
per activated customer.

34
00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.900
These measures use different denominators
and must retain their own labels.

35
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:51.523
Monthly transacting customers include
older acquisition cohorts and answer

36
00:01:51.523 --> 00:01:52.550
another question.

37
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.150
Now check reliability.

38
00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:58.659
Web-origin customers account for
ninety-five thousand completions from

39
00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:00.350
ninety-six thousand attempts.

40
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:04.556
Mobile-origin customers account for two
hundred and five thousand completions from

41
00:02:04.556 --> 00:02:06.850
two hundred and fourteen thousand
attempts.

42
00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:10.700
Add the completions and attempts before
dividing.

43
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:15.725
Three hundred thousand divided by three
hundred and ten thousand gives ninety-six

44
00:02:15.725 --> 00:02:17.400
point seven seven percent.

45
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.225
A simple average of the two origin
percentages would give the smaller

46
00:02:21.225 --> 00:02:22.500
group too much weight.

47
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.500
Incident duration in minutes is context;
it is not the denominator for

48
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.750
this transaction-success measure.

49
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.550
Compare June with May.

50
00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:35.669
Activation falls from forty-two to
thirty-eight percent, a decline of four

51
00:02:35.669 --> 00:02:36.600
percentage points.

52
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.800
That is different from a four percent
relative decline.

53
00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:44.788
Cost per verified customer rises from
fifty-four to sixty-six ringgit, a rise

54
00:02:44.788 --> 00:02:46.450
of about twenty-two percent.

55
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:51.204
Pause the lesson and compare revenue,
activation and success with the control

56
00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:51.600
card.

57
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.886
Open at least one original source location
in the app and explain

58
00:02:55.886 --> 00:02:56.600
its arithmetic.

59
00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:02.200
If a result differs, trace the source,
formula and scope before proceeding.

60
00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:06.000
Approve the contract only after those
checks reconcile.
